  (text "MAINS VOLTAGE ON EVERY NET EXCEPT PE. UNPLUG BEFORE TOUCHING." (at 30.48 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bdc49853-9396-52c9-ae23-3a56921e384a))
  (text "to the switch\nand back" (at 111.76 97.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 7e82adcf-3d87-5392-a1ca-5a7a8392c909))
  (text "motor leads" (at 252.73 71.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 53926904-3c8d-5964-964e-0b8dcbb44a55))
  (text "to a ring lug\non the top plate" (at 243.84 121.92 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 31837844-5383-5bd8-84cb-b3dccf3f2186))
  (text "How the circuit reads (XA service manual, page 3):\n- Line comes in on J1, goes through fuse F1, then out to the switch and back on J2.\n- C2 sits across the switch. After the switch the net is L_SW.\n- C1 goes from L_SW to the motor's RED lead.\n- The motor has four leads, paired by winding:\n  WHITE and RED are winding 1. WHITE and GREEN are winding 2.\n- GREEN always goes to neutral.\n\n120 V: fit JP1 and JP2 in position 1-2 (board: 120, link pointing left).\n  Winding 1 white goes to neutral. Winding 2 white goes to L_SW.\n  The windings are in parallel, with C1 in series with winding 1.\n220 V: fit JP1 and JP2 in position 2-3 (board: 220, link pointing up).\n  Winding 1 white goes to L_SW. Winding 2 white goes to RED.\n  The windings are in series, with C1 across winding 1.\nNever fit both positions on one jumper.\n\nTo confirm before power: the manual's 120 V drawing does not show where\nthe winding 1 white lead returns. Neutral is the reading used here\n(circuit logic and the under-plate picture). Check on an unmodified table." (at 30.48 187.96 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 8839d8d9-d925-567c-a454-e0ec12e935ad))
